sn22.80:10.9 starts: “… Is feeling constant or inconstant?”—“Inconstant, lord.” …
sn22.80:10.10 starts: “… Is perception constant or inconstant?”—“Inconstant, lord.” …
sn22.80:10.11 starts: “… Are fabrications constant or inconstant?”—“Inconstant, lord.” …
sn22.80:10.12 starts: “What do you think, monks? Is consciousness constant or inconstant?” “Inconstant, lord.” “And is that which is inconstant easeful or stressful?” “Stressful, lord.” “And is it fitting to regard what is inconstant, stressful, subject to change as: ‘This is mine. This is my self. This is what I am’?” “No, lord.” “Thus, monks, any form whatsoever that is past, future, or present; internal or external; blatant or subtle; common or sublime; far or near: Every form is to be seen as it has come to be with right discernment as: ‘This is not mine. This is not my self. This is not what I am.’ “Any feeling whatsoever.… “Any perception whatsoever.… “Any fabrications whatsoever.… “Any consciousness whatsoever that is past, future, or present; internal or external; blatant or subtle; common or sublime; far or near:
